WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
Detection engineering increasingly adopts software engineering practices.

2
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:16.802
Teams use version control, peer review, testing, documentation, change management, CI/CD workflows, and lifecycle processes to manage detection content more consistently.

3
00:00:16.802 --> 00:00:21.442
Detection-as-Code does not mean every organization needs the same toolchain.

4
00:00:21.442 --> 00:00:30.871
The core idea is that detections should be treated as controlled, reviewable, testable assets rather than informal edits made directly in a console.

5
00:00:30.871 --> 00:00:36.179
Version control helps teams understand what changed, who changed it, and why.

6
00:00:36.179 --> 00:00:41.457
Peer review improves quality by bringing additional context before logic reaches production.

7
00:00:41.457 --> 00:00:48.631
Testing helps teams validate detection behavior before deployment and after changes to data sources or platforms.

8
00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:56.933
Documentation helps analysts and engineers understand purpose, expected behavior, dependencies, and response guidance.

9
00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:01.134
Engineering practices also make detection programs easier to scale.

10
00:01:01.134 --> 00:01:10.782
As the number of detections grows, teams need consistent naming, ownership, metadata, review schedules, and release processes to keep the program maintainable.

11
00:01:10.782 --> 00:01:13.047
This approach supports safer change.

12
00:01:13.047 --> 00:01:24.302
When detection logic is reviewed, tested, and documented, teams are less likely to introduce avoidable noise, break existing coverage, or lose track of why a detection was created.

13
00:01:24.302 --> 00:01:26.317
It also makes onboarding easier.

14
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:36.445
New analysts and engineers can read the detection history, understand the intended behavior, and see how detections connect to telemetry sources and response workflows.

15
00:01:36.445 --> 00:01:39.588
Engineering discipline also supports accountability.

16
00:01:39.588 --> 00:01:51.541
Teams can define owners, service expectations, release steps, rollback options, and review cadences so detection content is managed with the same care as other production capabilities.
